.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_FEEDBACK_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_feedback_new ,
.Nm dtfl_feedback_connect
.Nd create a cycle in a dataflow
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_feedback_new "dtfl_scope *scope" "const dtfl_type *type" \
"const uint64_t *summary" "dtfl_feedback **handle"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_feedback_connect "dtfl_feedback *handle" "dtfl_stream *st"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A feedback edge turns a dataflow into a cycle: a stream whose contents
are supplied by a later part of the same computation.
.Fn dtfl_feedback_new
reserves a loop operator in
.Fa scope
with records of
.Fa type
and returns its output stream, before the source of that stream exists.
It stores a handle through
.Fa handle .
.Fa summary
is a path summary of the scope's class
.Pq Fn dtfl_summary_depth words
that is applied to every record's time as it re-enters the loop.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_feedback_connect
binds
.Fa st
as the loop operator's source and builds the operator, consuming the
handle.
Each record arriving on
.Fa st
is re-emitted on the loop stream with its time advanced by
.Fa summary ;
if the summary overflows the time's declared coordinate width, the
record is dropped, which is how a bounded loop stops.
A sound loop therefore uses a summary that strictly advances the loop
coordinate, so reachability sees that re-circulated data lands at a
later time and the frontier still advances.
.Pp
The loop stream is usually merged with a seed stream (for example with
.Fn dtfl_stream_concat )
before the merged stream is both consumed and fed back.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_feedback_new
returns the loop stream and stores the handle through
.Fa handle .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint64_t summary[DTFL_TIME_MAX];
dtfl_feedback *fb;

dtfl_summary_default(dtfl_scope_time_class(scope), summary);
summary[0] = 1;  /* advance the loop coordinate by one per lap */

dtfl_stream *cycle = dtfl_feedback_new(scope, dtfl_type_u64(),
    summary, &fb);
dtfl_stream *merged = dtfl_stream_concat(seed, cycle);
dtfl_stream *next = step_the_computation(merged);
dtfl_feedback_connect(fb, next);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_scope_iterative 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_summary_default 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt Feedback
and
.Vt ConnectLoop
traits and the
.Vt Handle
they share.
The
.Vt LoopVariable
trait is the same operator in an iterative scope, with the summary
wrapped in the inner coordinate.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The handle and the streams belong to the thread that runs the worker and
must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
Both calls run during the dataflow build, on that thread.
